__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
# data/satisfaction.csv is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, and that was wrong. The file holds the questionnaire responses, which
# are the only data in this project that cannot be regenerated by re-running a
# script -- and on a hosted free tier the container's filesystem is temporary,
# so a response written there is thrown away the next time the app sleeps.
# Ignoring the file meant the deployed app reported "No questionnaire responses
# yet" while Section 4.3 of the report analysed five of them.
#
# Committing it makes the reported figures reproducible from the repository and
# keeps the collected responses from being lost.
